y  but the main thing is to get rid of the  physical paperwork so that you save time  looking for them you save space and you  gain more clarity because you're not  drowning  in all this paperwork you can actually  have a clear open space to work in  please excuse my lighting it is 5 am as  i'm filming this so this is what i have  to work with  but typically what i have on my desk at  any given time  is a clock because i like to avoid  looking at my phone  when i'm working on something it's just  a distraction the current book that i'm  reading and a notebook  and then i have a little scripture verse  of course my computer  my speaker for youtube videos  and of course my printer and then on  this  cabinet is basically all of my office  supplies now everything that you might  need is  could be totally different but i have  some notebooks  this here is what i have limited myself  to as far as pens and pencils so i  had this just this old container and i  realized i did not need  a hundred different kinds of pens and  pencils and highlighters  so i limited myself to only this this  whatever fits in here  so in continuing to talk about office  supplies in general  i used to have a giant collection of  pens and pencils and highlighters  but for me i didn't need to have that  many  so look through the kinds of items that  you have and first of all check to make  sure that these pens even work because  they might not even work  but rather than having a specific number  of amount that you should have for any  kind of office supply  ask yourself how many you really need  for example you might be an artist so  you might need a lot of different  colored pencils  and supplies such as those for me i  don't do that particular work so i just  need just a few and this is probably a  little bit too much  next go through those items that you  haven't used in a while for example  six months to a year for me i had a  paper cutter  that i bought about four years ago and i  had used it like maybe three times since  then  that was clutter i did not need that and  for sentimental items such as  artwork that you or your kids have done  save these for last  if you can be happy without them and you  don't need them then  by all means declutter them but if  you're still kind of on the fence then  maybe one thing you can consider is  taking  pictures of these items instead that way  you keep the memory  but you don't keep the physical clutter  okay  i'm getting hungry how about we go to  the kitchen dinnerware is the next area  that we will cover and this includes  cups mugs plates and tupperware they say  the kitchen is the heart of the home  and a lot of us do spend a lot of time  in the kitchen i know personally with a  toddler i  certainly do and when i used to live  with my parents nothing used to annoy me  more than being in a rush to go to  school  opening the cabinet doors only to have  an avalanche of tupperware fall all over  me  or spend 10 minutes trying to find one  darn lid that would fit  any of those containers since we  decluttered our kitchen we've not only  been able to save time so we're not  spending 10 minutes looking for a lid  but it actually looks more appealing so  i'm not afraid if guests come over and i  open the cabinet doors  so let me show you our dinnerware  everything that we have in these  floating shelves and these cabinets is  basically all that we have for  dinnerware and then maybe just a few  that we're currently using  and yes i do have quite a lot of place  for just a family of three  soon to be four but for me it's  important to have extra  dinner plates and cups for when we have  visitors over because it saves a lot of  money and it saves the environment from  having to constantly be buying  disposable so one thing you will notice  is that a lot of these  items like the tupperware there these um  containers that we save from my  husband's favorite yogurts  the cups here and the plates stack very  well when we moved here i specifically  purchased items that would stack well  because we don't have a lot of cabinet  space  so this helps us to reduce clutter and  it saves a lot of precious space  also you will notice that i have a lot  of stainless steel cups and mason jars  i like these kinds of items because  they're very versatile they work for a  lot of different purposes  like mason jars can be used for drinking  they can be used for storing sauces  for storing berries yogurts meal  prepping oatmeal  even flower vases they probably have a  bajillion ways to be used  i also purchased these stainless steel  cups specifically because they stack so  well  and again we don't have a lot of cabinet  space so that is  a huge must for us but also they can be  used for hot and cold items  so we were able to toss our wine glasses  and use these instead  if you're interested in cups like these  i can include the link in the  description for these  so couple tips is you can have stackable  items to save space  have items that are versatile that you  can use for multiple purposes  but you'll also notice that i don't have  any souvenir cups holiday mugs or random  dinner plates  except for my blue cups it's all the  same color pretty much white  i did that intentionally to limit visual  clutter as well  so if you can try to stick with neutral  colors or just matching colors in  general  and do away with all of the holiday  decor souvenir cups and mugs and all  that kind of stuff  my tupperware is not eco-friendly it is  plastic but i've had it for about five  years now  the main thing that i would suggest to  you though is to find  one particular kind or brand that stacks  well  that way you're not having to look for  different kinds of lids for different  tupperwares and wasting so much time  so much clutter that's just crowding  your space  the next area of the home that a lot of  us could use a major declutter in  is probably the bathroom when i left  with my parents they had a huge  assortment of personal care items and  when they finally let me declutter it  i found items there from years ago that  had been expired  i bet you they had no idea that these  things were even there so go through  your bathroom and look through  every single item this part is important  so what you can do is remove  the cabinets and pour out all of the  items that are in there and go through  each of them one by one  look for these particular items expired  items  unused items from who knows when those  hotel freebies that you never used up  because why they're just collecting  space anyway  and if you have a favorite lotion or  perfume or just any kind of personal  care  product for example then you can  probably ditch all of the rest because  why have five different kinds if you  keep coming back to just one  i used to be notorious for having 10  different kinds of lipsticks but only  using one and rarely ever using the rest  so think of items like these for you and  get rid of those kinds of items  this next one may not necessarily apply  to you you may not want to do it and  that's totally okay  but i just want you to be aware of it  because i didn't know i got rid of all  the scented lotions and perfumes and  this one kind of hurt me it was the bath  and bodywork solutions because i got  great deals i mean you have to get the  deal right  so i had like 10 of these bottles that i  never even used  but i found out that these are harmful  and can actually cause cancer  because they have chemicals called  endocrine disruptors  so i tossed all those kinds of lotions  and i now only use coconut oil as lotion  and if i ever want a perfume then i use  essential oils if you're interested in  ridding your home of toxic chemicals  then perhaps i can do a video solely on  that because there's a lot to be said  about them and a lot of chemicals  that we aren't very aware of but i do  have a video on non-toxic personal care  swaps if you're interested  it's not very detailed i should have  done a better job it was one of my first  videos but there is some good  information in there for you  the next area of the home is not  necessarily an area but rather a group  of items and that is  items that require changing batteries  out or replacing the items frequently so  why do i even mention this in the first  place  because our lives are already hectic  enough to have to worry about little  details such as darn i can't use this  because i forgot to buy batteries or i  have to go to the store and get more  little things like that not only take up  our time but they're adding extra  expenses frequently  one example for us that frequently  caused an annoyance was that we had  purchased  wireless cameras and we knew upfront  that we were gonna have to replace  batteries on them but  at the time it seemed like a good idea  we were constantly having to replace  batteries about like  every two months and it was just getting  really annoying have to go to the store  just to buy the batteries  so we ended up finding a rechargeable  option for these things so now we don't  have to buy them  my suggestion would be that if you have  items that are like high dollar  that you don't want to necessarily get  rid of then try to find a replaceable  option or replaceable batteries for them  but if you can eliminate these items  altogether because they're just causing  more nuisance and hassle for you  so because there are numerous items that  can fall under this category i'm  actually planning on making a  separate video to talk about items that  you may have around the home that have a  reusable option for  not only can this save you money but it  can save you time as well so stick  around for that one  but for now let's head to the toy room  it might get a little loud in there  this is my kids toy collection minus a  few books or puzzles that i rotate out  and then maybe a couple odds and ends  scattered throughout the house  but i consider them very fortunate to  have all these toys for those of you who  are parents  oh boy you know how fun it is to pick up  toys constantly and then five minutes  later they're scattered all throughout  the floor again  i think this is why the meme i hope you  step on the lego came out  because those things hurt i grew up poor  i grew up in the middle of a desert but  yet i never lacked  toys to play kitchen for example i used  leaves  as my plates and mud as the taco meat i  used rocks to make houses and roads i  didn't need legos heck i didn't even  know they existed  i also remember making a dollhouse out  of an old box  the point that i'm trying to make here  is that because i didn't already have  the toys that did the work for me  i was able to imagine and create things  on my own  i think that when we load our kids with  flashy toys and gadgets we rob them of  their imagination to create these  experiences for themselves  and not only that but we're teaching  them at a young age that consumerism is  what will make them happy  so my tips for tackling kids toys are  these if your kids are young  go through the toys when they're not  around because even if that toy has been  in the corner of the room for months  they will want it only because you  picked it up if your kids are older go  through it with them  let them pick the favorites that they  want to keep and also have a  conversation with them  about sharing the toys that they will no  longer be using by donating them to  other children  this can be really difficult for them  especially if they're not used to it but  it can help them stretch their  decluttering muscle  and learn how to practice more  minimalism in their own life  to learn how to give and focus on giving  rather than receiving  it can also help them learn how to  practice more gratitude by learning how  to be happy with less  and for the toys that you do keep try to  keep open-ended toys that let them use  their imagination without flashy buttons  lights and sounds  for example i had a random cloth from a  dress that i had sewn and my daughter  loves this thing she uses it to wrap  gifts that she gives to us  she uses it as a scarf as a cover as a  cape  in many different ways so this would be  an example of an open-ended toy  if they have lots of toys with batteries  consider removing those not only does it  remove  them from having that constant attention  grabber  but it also prevents you from having to  go buy batteries because how annoying  and the last tip that i have for this  area is to consider letting your friends  and family know that you would like for  them to avoid purchasing gifts for your  kids  and if you have family members or  friends that would do it anyway  because i have some of those myself also  have a list of wish list toys for  example for me  that would be wooden toys or educational  activities  because someday i do want to homeschool  there are of course  many more ways to simplify your home so  if you have any suggestions  please leave them in the comments and if  you like this video please give it a  thumbs up and subscribe so that you  won't miss out on my weekly videos  i thank you so much for watching and i  can't wait to see you in the next one

